                <pb facs="0529" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 Steering Committee/223: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Delegate
                        (Wilson)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-12-06T14:00:00-05:00">December 6, 1932—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>259. Your 473, December 5, 10 p.m. Department has not received a copy of the
                    Japanese naval proposal. Please telegraph text if it is of reasonable length;
                    otherwise telegraph a summary and follow with full text by open mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
